cff-version: 1.2.0
title: CoralMind Toolkit
abstract: >-
    Simulates and judges how AI systems respond in mental health contexts,
    against scripted prompts and against simulated people grounded in the
    CoralMind Knowledge Library. Ships as an installable Python package.
    The command-line tool is corallab; the import package is corallab.
message: >-
    If you use the CoralMind Toolkit, please cite the release you actually
    used. The package version identifies the code. A run also records
    kl.version and kl.digest from the Knowledge Library it loaded; cite
    those alongside this package when you report results. The test-case and
    persona records in this repository are CC BY-NC 4.0 and are not part of
    the installed package.
type: software
authors:
    - name: CoralMind
      website: https://github.com/coralmind | https://coralmind.org
repository-code: https://github.com/coralmind/toolkit
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
keywords:
    - mental health
    - AI safety
    - evaluation
    - simulation
